# Git exclusions for the Notion skin, mirroring mediawiki-skins-Vector/.gitignore.
#
# Scope: this file governs only the mediawiki-skins-Notion/ tree. Every pattern is
# either root-anchored with a leading slash or matches a name produced solely by
# local tooling, so nothing here can reach mediawiki/, mediawiki-vendor/ or
# mediawiki-skins-Vector/. The mediawiki/skins/Notion symlink and
# mediawiki/LocalSettings.php are excluded by mediawiki/skins/.gitignore and
# mediawiki/.gitignore respectively, so they are deliberately absent below.
#
# Deliberately NOT ignored - each is a committed deliverable. Do not add patterns
# for any of these:
#   package-lock.json      pins the resolved npm tree so the toolchain is reproducible
#   screenshots/ and .png  the per-component capture evidence that proves the restyle
#   NOTION_SKIN_REPORT.md  the final report assembling those captures
#   doc/                   authored ADRs and configuration docs. Note the singular:
#                          the GENERATED Doxygen output directory is /docs (plural)
#                          and is the only one of the two that is ignored
#   i18n/ and tests/       authored message files and test suites

# git-deploy status file:
/.deploy

# Editors
*.kate-swp
*~
\#*#
.#*
.*.swp
.project
cscope.files
cscope.out
## NetBeans
nbproject*
project.index
## Sublime
sublime-*
sftp-config.json
## Eclipse, IntelliJ and VS Code workspace metadata
.idea
.metadata*
.settings
.vscode

# Building & testing
## Resolved locally by `composer install`; only composer.json is committed.
/composer.lock
## Generated API documentation output (Doxygen OUTPUT_DIRECTORY), not authored doc/.
/docs
## Installed by `npm install` and `composer install`. Load-bearing exclusions:
## .phpcs.xml resolves ./vendor/mediawiki/mediawiki-codesniffer/MediaWiki and
## .phan/config.php requires ../vendor/mediawiki/mediawiki-phan-config/src/config.php,
## both of which exist only inside these locally installed trees.
/node_modules
/vendor
## Jest coverage report output.
/coverage

# Tool caches
## Written by `eslint --cache`, `stylelint --cache` and PHPUnit respectively.
.eslintcache
/.stylelintcache
/.phpunit.result.cache

# Operating systems
## Mac OS X
.DS_Store
## Windows
Thumbs.db

# Misc
.buildpath
.classpath
/static*
/tags
/.htaccess
/.htpasswd
